---
description: Compare the actual measure or obligation observed in a pair, accounting for explicit revisions and dates.
args:
  goal: string
  pair: SourceReceipt[]
returns: ResearchDisposition
---
Use superseded only when a source explicitly revises or supersedes the earlier relevant value for that same subject and interval. A newer publication date alone does not establish a replacement. Use incomparable when scopes, units, cohorts or events differ and the receipts do not bridge them. Use corroborated when both establish the same relevant claim with compatible scope, conflicting when they establish different claims for the same scope, and unresolved when either passage does not present a directly comparable assertion.
